  "step_3": "The decision reason is based on variance, which depends on both the magnitude of the loss and the probability of the loss. The individual did not consider variance or the probability-weighted square of the loss. Instead, the individual focused on the absolute size of the loss (6000 vs. 3000), noting that the loss in B is smaller. This reflects a different reasoning—comparing loss magnitude—rather than evaluating risk dispersion. Since the verbal report does not mention variance, probabilities of loss, or any calculation involving squared deviations, the decision reason was not used. The individual’s justification is inconsistent with the variance-based rule.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
